  "text" : "A flop is one multiplier, one add, and it's the unit that all AI compute is measured in.\nFlop stands for floating point operation.\nComputers store decimals as a floating point, scientific notation in binary, a sign, digits,\nand an exponent.\nThe point floats, so one format holds a ten millionth and three millionth.\nEvery weight, activation, and gradient is one of these numbers.\nFlops with a small s is a count.\nTraining an 8 billion parameter model on 15,000 tokens costs about 720 trillion flops.\nFlops with a capital S is per second.\nThis is a rate.\nA B200 peaks near 2250 teraflops in BF16.\nTera is a trillion.\nA transformer's compute is nearly all matrix multiplies and a matmul is only multiplies\nand adds.\nGPUs are built to do exactly that.\nThousands at once.\nA divider runs flops.\nBuy the flops.\nget and you have GPU hours. This is the bill."
}
